{"id":"416b3745e60b0423","group":"58","path":"58/batch20/58-thm-compactness.md","title":"Compactness Theorem","display":"thm-compactness — Compactness Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-compactness","aliases":["58-thm-compactness","Compactness Theorem","First-Order Compactness"],"display":"thm-compactness — Compactness Theorem","depends_on":["[[58-df-language]]","[[58-df-theory]]","[[58-df-formula]]","[[58-df-satisfaction]]","[[58-df-finite]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-compactness"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-compactness</span><span>Compactness Theorem</span><span>First-Order Compactness</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-compactness — Compactness Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"d81b1b2123168018\" href=\"?note=d81b1b2123168018\" title=\"58-df-language\">58-df-language</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"90ce6acf0c65af45\" href=\"?note=90ce6acf0c65af45\" title=\"58-df-theory\">58-df-theory</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"58-df-formula\">58-df-formula</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"8b6a90316aad78a4\" href=\"?note=8b6a90316aad78a4\" title=\"58-df-satisfaction\">58-df-satisfaction</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"d9a25b0ac94a3598\" href=\"?note=d9a25b0ac94a3598\" title=\"58-df-finite\">58-df-finite</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L,T,T_0,\\mathcal M\\in V\">\\(L,T,T_0,\\mathcal M\\in V\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Theory}(T,L)\">\\(\\mathrm{Theory}(T,L)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Model}(\\mathcal M,T)\">\\(\\mathrm{Model}(\\mathcal M,T)\\)</span> are the exact source predicates.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Finite}(T_0)\">\\(\\mathrm{Finite}(T_0)\\)</span> is the registered finite-set predicate.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}compactness}\\vdash \\Bigl[\\mathrm{Theory}(T,L)\\land\\forall T_0\\in\\mathcal P(T)\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Finite}(T_0)\\to\\exists\\mathcal M_{T_0}\\in V\\;\\mathrm{Model}(\\mathcal M_{T_0},T_0)\\bigr)\\Bigr]\\to\\exists\\mathcal M\\in V\\;\\mathrm{Model}(\\mathcal M,T).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}compactness}\\vdash \\Bigl[\\mathrm{Theory}(T,L)\\land\\forall T_0\\in\\mathcal P(T)\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Finite}(T_0)\\to\\exists\\mathcal M_{T_0}\\in V\\;\\mathrm{Model}(\\mathcal M_{T_0},T_0)\\bigr)\\Bigr]\\to\\exists\\mathcal M\\in V\\;\\mathrm{Model}(\\mathcal M,T).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Compactness discovered independently by Gödel and Malcev.</li>\n<li>Finite subtheories are bounded by <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal P(T)\">\\(\\mathcal P(T)\\)</span> and tested by the sourced finiteness predicate rather than an undefined cardinality comparison.</li>\n<li>Equivalent to Boolean Prime Ideal Theorem (for propositional logic).</li>\n<li>In a countable language, a satisfiable theory has a model of cardinality at most <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\aleph_0\">\\(\\aleph_0\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>A model can be chosen of size at most <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\max(|L|,\\aleph_0)\">\\(\\max(|L|,\\aleph_0)\\)</span> when an infinite model is required.</li>\n<li>Compactness is tightly related to completeness and soundness.</li>\n<li>Applications: model theory, nonstandard analysis, algebra.</li>\n<li>Creates nonstandard models: infinite integers, infinitesimals.</li>\n<li>Compactness + Löwenheim-Skolem: basis of model theory.</li>\n<li>Countable compactness: uses less choice than uncountable case.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-language","status":"resolved","id":"d81b1b2123168018","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-language]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-theory","status":"resolved","id":"90ce6acf0c65af45","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-theory]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-formula","status":"resolved","id":"65418b505fc53093","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-formula]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-satisfaction","status":"resolved","id":"8b6a90316aad78a4","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-satisfaction]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-finite","status":"resolved","id":"d9a25b0ac94a3598","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-finite]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"L,T,T_0,\\mathcal M\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Theory}(T,L)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Model}(\\mathcal M,T)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Finite}(T_0)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}compactness}\\vdash \\Bigl[\\mathrm{Theory}(T,L)\\land\\forall T_0\\in\\mathcal P(T)\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Finite}(T_0)\\to\\exists\\mathcal M_{T_0}\\in V\\;\\mathrm{Model}(\\mathcal M_{T_0},T_0)\\bigr)\\Bigr]\\to\\exists\\mathcal M\\in V\\;\\mathrm{Model}(\\mathcal M,T).